IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4, ss 43-62 (part ssc3).
-- THE HELPERS: three-valued "and" and "or" over MAYBE BOOLEAN, and nothing else.
--
-- Departure from PLAN.md section 1.2, recorded in NOTES.md: these two names do not begin with a
-- section label, because they implement no provision. They begin `ssc3 helper`, which no other
-- part can define, so the purpose of the naming rule (no two modules share a name) is kept.
--
-- Why they exist: a rule of the form "A and B and C" in which one fact is NOTHING must answer
-- FALSE when another fact is FALSE (the text's "no" does not wait for the unknown fact) and NOTHING
-- otherwise; collapsing NOTHING into FALSE is forbidden by the FALSE and NOTHING rule of 2026-10-29.

§ `Helpers: three-valued logic`

-- The conjunction of a list of facts, each TRUE, FALSE or not covered.
-- FALSE if any fact is FALSE; otherwise NOTHING if any fact is NOTHING; otherwise TRUE.
-- The empty list is TRUE (nothing is required).
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ssc3 helper all of` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN fact YIELD fact EQUALS JUST FALSE) facts THEN JUST FALSE
        IF any (GIVEN fact YIELD fact EQUALS NOTHING) facts THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The disjunction of a list of facts.
-- TRUE if any fact is TRUE; otherwise NOTHING if any fact is NOTHING; otherwise FALSE.
-- The empty list is FALSE (nothing holds).
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ssc3 helper any of` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN fact YIELD fact EQUALS JUST TRUE) facts THEN JUST TRUE
        IF any (GIVEN fact YIELD fact EQUALS NOTHING) facts THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- A plain fact as a three-valued one.
GIVEN fact IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ssc3 helper known` MEANS JUST fact

-- The negation of a three-valued fact: NOTHING stays NOTHING.
GIVEN fact IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ssc3 helper not` MEANS
    CONSIDER fact
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST value THEN JUST (NOT value)

-- The date on which a person's age is reached is not computed here (s 173 is the keel's):
-- a tax year is named by the calendar year in which it begins (6 April).
-- The tax year, as the year in which it begins, that contains a date.
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ssc3 helper tax year of` MEANS
    IF day AT LEAST (Date 6 4 (DATE_YEAR day))
    THEN DATE_YEAR day
    ELSE (DATE_YEAR day) MINUS 1

-- The first day of the tax year that begins in a calendar year.
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`ssc3 helper first day of tax year` MEANS Date 6 4 year

-- The sum of amounts some of which may be not covered: NOTHING if any is NOTHING, else the sum.
-- An amount is never invented for a NOTHING.
GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`ssc3 helper sum of` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN x YIELD x EQUALS NOTHING) xs
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (sum (map (GIVEN x YIELD fromMaybe 0 x) xs))
